{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Fish: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja75'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 75 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Varuṇavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Warding Tree </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>5. Macchajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Fish: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Abhitthanaya pajjunna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Thunder forth, Pajjuna! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nidhiṁ kākassa nāsaya; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Disperse the trove of the crow! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kākaṁ sokāya randhehi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Subject the crow to sorrow, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mañca sokā pamocayā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and free me from sorrow! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Macchajātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
